Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.73,0:00:08.73,Karaoke Translation op,TITLE,0,0,0,,{\3c&H000000&\pos(234,874)}Final Episode
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.73,0:00:08.73,Karaoke Translation op,TITLE,0,0,0,,{\3c&H000000&\pos(292,1042)}Earth, the Yamato is…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.22,0:00:25.53,def2,MINA,0,0,0,,The floating fragments of Area 550 have \Ntaken a descending trajectory into the Moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.53,0:00:28.39,def2,MINA,0,0,0,,Moving on to Area 551.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.07,0:00:30.83,def2,MEGUMI,0,0,0,,Reload magnetron probes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.48,0:00:33.49,def2,MINA,0,0,0,,Reloading magnetron probes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.31,0:00:35.66,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,What a mess…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.48,0:00:40.94,def2,ROBOT,0,0,0,,Current moon surface rebuild rate, 7.5%.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.53,0:00:49.03,def2,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(962,642)}A half year since the war with Gatlantis…
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.83,0:01:25.98,def2,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&H1484B8&\pos(958,698)}Okita Juzo
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.88,0:01:50.88,def2,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H1484B8&\frz5.486\move(1278,686,1266,432,41,1960)}Commander
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.52,0:01:54.02,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Promotion, huh ?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.48,0:02:30.29,def2,MAN,0,0,0,,It's the Yamato.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.66,0:02:41.83,def2,TODO,0,0,0,,That's correct, Mr. Sanada. \NYou pick the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.14,0:02:46.63,def2,TODO,0,0,0,,I want you to find out what's going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.63,0:02:51.35,def2,TODO,0,0,0,,It's hard to believe,\N but if it's really the Yamato…
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.42,0:02:58.59,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Kodai !
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.63,0:03:02.82,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Kodai…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.26,0:03:08.41,def2,YAMAZAKI,0,0,0,,{\c&HF7FDAB&}This is Yamazaki !\N I found a survivor !
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.18,0:03:17.38,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,It's alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.32,0:03:19.53,def2,YAMAZAKI,0,0,0,,Over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.47,0:03:27.87,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,Yamamoto !
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.53,0:03:38.82,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,There you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.40,0:03:45.47,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}Two sets of memories merge…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.70,0:03:49.03,def2,TOUKO,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anything can happen here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.39,0:03:51.51,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.34,0:03:53.51,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.97,0:04:01.06,def2,KATO,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's a projection. \NKodai's over there right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.13,0:04:06.33,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,I saw a tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.14,0:04:10.61,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,It was so big that I couldn't \Nsee the top or its base.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.22,0:04:16.15,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,{teresa}That's how Teresa sees\N the flow of time, she says.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.22,0:04:20.98,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,{moshika}Maybe that's Teresa herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.98,0:04:22.28,def2,BARREL,0,0,0,,Did you talk to Teresa ?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.72,0:04:27.93,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,No, it could have been my brother, \NTsurumi, or even Klaus.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.90,0:04:32.48,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Things like who or where \Nare ambiguous in that world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.18,0:04:38.07,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,But I was asked to relay her message, \Nand I remember it clearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.33,0:04:43.78,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Those two could have come home\Nif they wished, but they didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.88,0:04:45.64,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,That's why…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.58,0:04:56.33,def2,BARREL,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&H9B9B9B&\pos(1176,662)}Klaus Keyman
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.64,0:04:55.62,def2,BARREL,0,0,0,,Klaus was tossed left and right by his fate, but he achieved salvation by going onboard the Yamato and meeting you. {TEXT: Klaus Keyman}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.28,0:05:04.01,def2,BARREL,0,0,0,,It's not going to be easy, but I'll do \Nmy best to respond to her message.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.53,0:05:12.28,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,When the Ark of Destruction disappeared...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.28,0:05:17.92,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,...a tremendous energy was released,\N but it didn't have any impact on Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.55,0:05:21.73,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,Teresa merged with the Yamato...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.73,0:05:25.92,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,...and pushed the annihilation energy \Naway beyond the dimensional horizon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.68,0:05:28.98,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{sou}That makes sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.94,0:05:34.58,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{sono}The reaction pushed the \NYamato into a higher dimension.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.70,0:05:37.38,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,The basis for your argument is weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.23,0:05:40.60,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,It's just one surviving pilot, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.26,0:05:43.88,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,Nevertheless, I'm with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.95,0:05:47.30,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,So many have died.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.26,0:05:53.70,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,We don't have enough crews. \NYet, we keep building ships.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.60,0:06:04.88,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,No matter what the future holds for Earth, \Neveryone's come to realize the path is unfavorable.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.16,0:06:13.90,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,We found a dimensional node deep behind \Nthe water wall where the Yamato surfaced.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.16,0:06:18.93,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{jikan}There's another fault deep \Nwithin the Time Fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.02,0:06:27.63,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{yamato}In the deepest fault, time has been so infinitely stretched that humans can't measure it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.63,0:06:34.52,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{modottekita}The Yamato's come back from that fault, leaving \NCaptain Kodai and Operational Chief Mori behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.30,0:06:37.01,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,Do you mean…
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.01,0:06:39.35,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,Yes, they're both alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.96,0:06:49.88,def2,YAMAMOTO,0,0,0,,I've been sent to relay a message that the course of\N the future will return to normal by bringing them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.88,0:06:52.18,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,How could that be possible ?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.18,0:06:56.68,def2,TODO,0,0,0,,Is it possible to back track\Nthe route the Yamato has taken ?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.05,0:07:03.79,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,It doesn't require any energy to descend\N from a higher dimension to our dimension.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.36,0:07:07.43,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,However, in order for us to ascend…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.43,0:07:12.24,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,…simply put, we need near infinite energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.22,0:07:14.24,def2,TODO,0,0,0,,Infinite…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.01,0:07:19.15,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,Then, we have no means…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.15,0:07:20.20,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,We still have a way…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.70,0:07:25.61,def2,YAMANAMI…with,0,0,0,,...with the help of the Ginga.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.55,0:07:29.48,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,The damage would be severe...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.48,0:07:35.86,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,...but if we use the Ginga's CRS amplifier again,\N we can compress the excess dimensions of the fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.59,0:07:40.76,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,In other words, we induce a collapse\N of dimensions inside the fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.76,0:07:47.38,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{sono}Using the collapsing force to launch \Nthe Yamato into the higher dimension.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.38,0:07:50.38,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,The Time Fault would be like\N a balloon with a sudden loss of air.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.46,0:07:54.17,def2,YAMANAMI,0,0,0,,It'll collapse and disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.16,0:07:56.63,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,How absurd !
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.08,0:08:03.18,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,It's a tall order to sacrifice the \NTime Fault to save two people, isn't it ?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.78,0:08:06.73,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,Yeah. \NIt's totally unreasonable.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.73,0:08:12.74,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,But on the political side, a miracle might \Noccur thanks to Ambassador Barrel's efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.89,0:08:17.33,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{kondo}The last war shocked the political scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.33,0:08:21.63,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{subete}Reveal everything and\N call for a national vote…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.63,0:08:24.98,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,The impossible might actually happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.04,0:08:27.44,def2,SAKI,0,0,0,,National vote ?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.02,0:08:33.32,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,We can't swing the vote, and\N the odds are still against us.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.94,0:08:38.18,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,But what if that can correct\N the path of the future ?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.18,0:08:43.21,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,We might be being tested.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.82,0:08:48.49,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,Kodai, what're you doing now ?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.36,0:09:08.38,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}The planets only stay in their locations.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.34,0:09:14.17,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only you can turn them \Ninto meaningful entities…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.11,0:09:20.50,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{utsukushii}…with the heart to admire their beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.37,0:09:30.75,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{kokoro}Your soul nurtures love,\N and love resonates to build fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.78,0:09:38.08,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{sorera}It becomes entwined with many to \Nweave what you call time and space.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.75,0:09:42.68,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}But excessive love can sometimes…
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.22,0:09:47.53,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can still see your future.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.84,0:09:52.45,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, open your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.68,0:10:01.07,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Things could have been different.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.59,0:10:07.34,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Things can be different.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.14,0:10:11.94,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{subete}Everything's determined by your desire.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.68,0:10:16.27,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{nozomeba}You can have your ideal world if you so wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.27,0:10:19.75,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,But I pulled the trigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.41,0:10:27.61,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,And I'll keep losing precious things \Nby repeating the same action.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.78,0:10:38.34,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,Please take a look at the night scenery of the\N capital, which has been restored thus far.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.34,0:10:41.63,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,Energy, material, military power…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.63,0:10:45.11,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,All of them are crucial for our future.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.03,0:10:49.48,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,And it's all supported by the Time Fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.29,0:10:54.40,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,Consider the meaning of destroying it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.18,0:10:58.53,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,We should put all our emotions aside...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.53,0:11:04.05,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,...and take the next 100 years of Earth's \Nprosperity into account, before making a decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.86,0:11:08.97,def2,AIHARA,0,0,0,,Shima, aren't you going\N to hear the next speech ?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.64,0:11:11.00,def2,SHIMA,0,0,0,,We've got things to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.39,0:11:14.31,def2,NANBU,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.31,0:11:15.06,def2,HOSHINA,0,0,0,,Yuria…
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.06,0:11:15.82,def2,YURIA,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.82,0:11:17.16,def2,YAMAZAKI,0,0,0,,It's the third hangar.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.17,0:11:18.85,def2,MIKAGE,0,0,0,,It's all ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.85,0:11:19.88,def2,SHINOHARA,0,0,0,,Let's get going.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.26,0:11:25.26,def2,SERIZAWA,0,0,0,,I envy you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.92,0:11:38.55,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,Let me talk about a man.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.03,0:11:44.28,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,He's an ordinary man \Nyou can find anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.07,0:11:48.40,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{hito}He loves people, and believes\Nin the society built by people.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.31,0:11:55.59,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{chikyuu}When Earth faced the danger of destruction, he joined the great journey to Iscandar.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.83,0:12:04.22,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{soshite}After returning home, he broke his back for the \Nrestoration of Earth just like each and every one of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.86,0:12:11.39,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{kare}His only wish was to keep\N our promise with Iscandar.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.19,0:12:16.79,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{shikashi}However, the situation of the post-war\NEarth didn't allow him to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.88,0:12:21.68,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{uragirareta}He must have felt the\N sense of betrayal.{unfaithfulness.}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.70,0:12:26.01,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{dakara}That's why, when we received\Na message from Telezart…
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.48,0:12:29.14,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{karewa}…he didn't hesitate to respond, despite\N the risk of being accused of revolt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.01,0:12:34.98,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{uchuu}He wanted to be faithful to his belief that we, the people of Earth, should keep the peace of the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.96,0:12:44.58,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{shikashi}In the end, he had to pull the trigger of the wave \Nmotion gun more frequently than anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.00,0:12:52.42,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{ikiru}In order to survive, in order to protect, \Nhe had to betray what was in his heart.{'s been unfaithful to his heart.}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.89,0:12:58.98,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{muron}He did try to resist, using every \Navailable opportunity to seek peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.98,0:13:04.93,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{jibun}He even stood in front of an enemy \Nwho was pointing a gun at him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.61,0:13:14.06,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{shikashi}But everything turned out negatively, \Nand he had to turn his life into a weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.69,0:13:19.37,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{sorede}It saved Earth, but that's just hindsight.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.58,0:13:28.53,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{karewa}He, and Mori Yuki, who loved him\Nand met the same fate, are not heroes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.09,0:13:32.63,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{karewa}He's you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.63,0:13:38.41,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{yumemita}Failing to realize our dreams, \Nwe feel the sense of loss every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.35,0:13:45.23,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{ikiru}We're used to deceiving ourselves in\N the name of survival and responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.23,0:13:47.86,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{hontou}We've lost our true selves.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.18,0:13:56.63,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{kinou}Even though we know yesterday's mistake\N and today's compromise will erode our future…
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.63,0:13:59.50,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{dokoe}…we keep walking on the\N path which leads to nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.66,0:14:08.96,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{kono}He's another self of you and I,\N who must live through this difficult time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.32,0:14:14.02,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{desukara}That's why you shouldn't feel obliged.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.14,0:14:21.19,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{eiyuu}It's wrong to think that the sacrifice is\Njustifiable just because they're heroes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.03,0:14:27.38,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{moshi}If you think you can save\N yourself by saving them…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.16,0:14:34.36,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{kono}…if you think this absurd choice\N can lead to our true future…
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.45,0:14:39.54,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{zehi}…then please vote to rescue both of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.35,0:14:47.40,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{tuujiau}Please don't let the voices for convenience and\N efficiency deceive you, but follow your heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.48,0:14:54.00,def2,SANADA,0,0,0,,{mirai}That's our only future.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.63,0:14:58.88,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.88,0:15:03.38,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's branched out so widely \Nthat it'll eventually dry up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.38,0:15:04.58,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Dry up ?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.58,0:15:09.98,def2,TOKUGAWA,0,0,0,,{\i1}There must be a force so strong \Nthat it can break the flow of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.98,0:15:13.03,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Even though the\N Ark of Destruction was destroyed ?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.03,0:15:14.85,def2,SAITO,0,0,0,,{\i1}That wasn't enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.45,0:15:19.88,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}Intelligent life-forms, like humans, \Nhave a great responsibility to the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.88,0:15:24.73,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}{sonotame}We're given a mechanism called a soul\N to fulfill it, but it's complex and fragile.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.94,0:15:30.56,def2,KEYMAN,0,0,0,,{\i1}{tokini}Sometimes it nurtures despair,\N and halts our walk forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.31,0:15:32.45,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai !
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.01,0:15:36.22,def2,HIJIKATA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kodai.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.52,0:15:41.18,def2,OKITA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kodai{\i1}, how much longer are you going to be like that ?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.18,0:15:41.98,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai !
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.63,0:15:44.95,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai, come over here !
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.28,0:15:48.64,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Yuki, no, I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.83,0:15:51.98,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,{donna}No matter how hard I try\N to find a different future…
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.32,0:15:59.98,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,{hikigane}…only the perpetual cycle of\N pulling the trigger is left for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.98,0:16:00.93,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,No !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.86,0:16:04.81,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,I don't want this sense \Nof loss anymore, so…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.02,0:16:08.99,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,I don't want it either, so Kodai…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.59,0:16:12.26,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.91,0:16:20.00,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,Kodai Susumu saved Earth !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.51,0:16:22.53,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,He did it before...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.43,0:16:28.53,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,...and he will do it \Nover and over again !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.53,0:16:31.23,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,{donna}No matter how badly he's beaten...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.23,0:16:34.98,def2,YUKI,0,0,0,,...he'll always do that because\N he has Mori Yuki by his side !
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.42,0:16:59.42,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's one of many futures.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.38,0:17:04.63,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it's the only future that awaits you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.63,0:17:06.08,def2,KODAI,0,0,0,,Future…
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.14,0:17:35.43,def2,MILL,0,0,0,,{\i1}The path to the future is restored.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.43,0:17:37.98,def2,TOUKO,0,0,0,,{\i1}The future will eventually be gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.98,0:17:44.23,def2,TOUKO,0,0,0,,{\i1}The universe will eventually use up\N its energy, then cool down and die.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.23,0:17:46.67,def2,TOUKO,0,0,0,,{\i1}But that's not everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.82,0:18:35.08,def2,MILL,0,0,0,,{\i1}Life and human intelligence can re-create it…
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.08,0:18:37.67,def2,MILL,0,0,0,,{\i1}{saisei}…as long as we envision\N the universe in our souls.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.14,0:18:43.24,def2,TOUKO,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's the duty of humans, who\N know how to love with their hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.09,0:18:49.98,def2,MILL,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eternal warmth keeps\N on protecting the universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.74,0:18:57.55,def2,KO,0,0,0,,Let's go home, Yuki.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.26,0:19:12.44,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}The planets only stay in their locations.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.51,0:19:18.15,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}Only humans can turn them\Ninto meaningful entities…
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.62,0:19:22.58,def2,TERESA,0,0,0,,{\i1}{utsukushii}…with the heart to admire their beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.98,0:23:51.61,def2,NARRATOR,0,0,0,,{\i1}In the infinitely expansive universe, \Nthere exists various kinds of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.38,0:23:57.34,def2,NARRATOR,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stars die and stars arise.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.31,0:24:04.28,def2,NARRATOR,0,0,0,,{\i1}The heartbeat of this vast universe is \Npassed on from one life to another...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.28,0:24:07.96,def2,NARRATOR,0,0,0,,{\i1}...and it will never come to an end.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.08,0:24:13.28,Karaoke Translation op,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\pos(456,402)}Space Battleship
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.08,0:24:13.28,def2,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(1260,762)}Soldiers of Love
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.08,0:24:13.28,yamato,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\fscx347\fscy257\\pos(806,856)} Yamato
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.48,0:24:19.23,def2,TEXT,0,0,0,,{\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(956,708)}The End
